* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɑtli/|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|mot|ley}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|more|motlier|motleyer}}

# Comprising greatly [[varied]] [[element]]s, to the point of [[incongruity]].
#: {{syn|en|heterogeneous|diverse|manifold|Thesaurus:heterogeneous}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare As You Like It|act=II|scene=vii|lines=906–907|passage=I met a fool i' th' forest, / A '''motley'''' fool.}}
#* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=II|passage=Carried somehow, somewhither, for some reason, on these surging floods, were these travelers,{{nb...}}. Even such a boat as the ''Mount Vernon'' offered a total deck space so cramped as to leave secrecy or privacy well out of the question, even had the '''motley''' and democratic assemblage of passengers been disposed to accord either.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=HarryBlank|work=w:SCP Foundation|title=Working Wonders|date=24 September 2023|url=https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/26-working-wonders|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240525140823/https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/26-working-wonders|archivedate=25 May 2024|accessdate=25 May 2024|text="One of them can see you, and one of them can see an empty hallway." Reynders narrowed her bleary eyes — she wasn't wearing her glasses, for some reason — as though momentarily uncertain which sight she was seeing. She apparently decided in favour of their '''motley''' group. "I'm the one who can see you. The one who can see you can talk to you. The one who can't talk to you can see you too, sometimes, but she doesn't want to because she knows you're not there. Where she is."}}
# Having many [[colour]]s; [[variegated]].
#: {{synonyms|en|colorful|prismatic|variegated|Thesaurus:multicolored}}

